  "configuration_id": "config_024",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) at 0.619 acc. Key learnings: (1) multimodal >> rna_only, (2) multiprofile >> singleprofile (largest single gain), (3) avgpool > transformer for aggregation, (4) concat ≈ weighted for fusion. The two major untested dimensions in the best config are the image encoder (resnet50 vs imagenet_vit_l) and the RNA encoder (pca vs learned). Question: Does upgrading the image encoder from ResNet50 to a much larger ViT-L improve performance in the already-optimized multiprofile+avgpool+concat setup? Why this is the best next experiment: The image modality has been the single largest source of improvement (multimodal vs rna_only), and ViT-L represents a substantial capacity jump over ResNet50. Testing it in the known-best configuration isolates the image encoder variable cleanly. If it helps, we've identified a new promising axis; if not, we rule out image encoder quality as a bottleneck and can redirect budget toward RNA encoder choices (scvi/scgpt) with greater confidence."
}

